From 64199e6d44dc99bc1789c50ef19e401eaa0e37bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:29:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] style(departments): make the head portrait float like an
 article, not a rigid column
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adopts the layout mechanism from the epr.rw reference the team has been
matching stylistically (passport-style head card) — but properly, using
a genuine CSS float instead of a fixed two-column grid.

The department head card now floats top-right of the Overview section
and the "About <dept>" copy and Key Activities list wrap around it, the
way a magazine profile wraps text around a portrait. Once the copy runs
past the bottom of the card it reclaims the full article width, instead
of being permanently squeezed into a fixed column regardless of length.
On mobile/tablet the card stays stacked full-width above the copy, since
a float only cramps things at narrow widths.

No visual changes to the head card itself — it keeps the team's current
styling (rounded-none, black name, no "Department Head" label, 280px
width) untouched; only the surrounding layout mechanism changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012xNEugH42JGJDBqiHFtfyU
